          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tēctum is the past participle of tegō, \"to cover\", used as a noun: \"what covers\" (Lewis & Short). tegō is usually traced to Proto-Indo-European (s)teg-, \"to cover with a roof\" (EtymDB 2.1); English thatch is a cousin."
            }
          ]
        },
